# Work tracking (ideas + Issues)

| Kind of knowledge | Where |
|-------------------|-------|
| Design intent, decisions, alternatives, and unresolved questions | Owning note in `docs/ideas/` |
| Actionable build work | GitHub Issue |
| Current focus | `docs/NOW.md` |

## Preserve consequential design discussions

Search for the owning note first and use the [idea template](../../docs/ideas/_template.md).
Proactively capture a durable idea, meaningful fork, or decision before the context
is lost. Do this in the related note update, design handoff, or PR when practical.
A short dated entry is enough. Skip passing hypotheticals and avoid separate PRs
for minor thoughts. Add an index link when a new owning note is needed.

Record the reason and known tradeoffs alongside the alternatives. An implemented
choice does not imply another option was rejected. Keep unapproved ideas proposed,
and preserve conflicting ideas with their status and relationship visible. Use
explicit author approval to mark a design accepted, rejected, or superseded.
When superseded, link the dated records both ways and preserve the earlier
reasoning. If a discussion or source cannot be recovered, say what is unknown.

## Check design before implementation

The author owns lore, characterization, and intended experience. Mechanics that
change world rules, progression, balance, or capabilities are collaborative.
Agents own technical choices that preserve agreed behaviour and compatibility.

Before implementing a gameplay change and again before opening its PR, compare
the proposed behaviour with relevant accepted design notes and current code and
test contracts. If it conflicts with an accepted rule or materially narrows
the intended experience, show the author the evidence, explain the divergence
in plain language, and identify the gain, sacrifice, affected systems, and
compatibility risks. Ask for a focused decision before committing to that
gameplay direction. Independent technical investigation can continue. An
unimplemented aspiration or a newer exploratory idea does not by itself create
or supersede an accepted rule. Routine fixes that restore an established
contract can proceed. If the evidence leaves a consequential creative or
mechanical choice open, ask about that choice instead of settling it silently.

## Queue and ship the agreed slice

1. Open an Issue for the next authorized implementation slice or prerequisite and
   link it with the owning note. Open Issues for unapproved ideas only when
   explicitly requested. Update `NOW.md` when current focus changes.
2. Open the PR with the [branch and handoff guidance](github-branch-workflow.mdc).
3. On merge, close the relevant Issue and update only the affected topic and
   implementation slice. Link to PR and test evidence. Distinguish proposed work,
   a landed prototype, partial implementation, completion within stated scope,
   and known divergence. A merge does not approve a design, implement deferred
   scope, or resolve alternatives. Preserve unresolved options, past reasoning,
   and deferred work in the owning note.
